;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; Gauntlet drops: things that fall out of the sky onto Jak on request, on any
;; level. The request is a file, Mods/gauntlet-drop-request.txt, whose first word
;; is a counter and whose second names what to drop ("7 bomb"). A counter that
;; changed since the last look is a new request; a name this file does not know
;; is logged and dropped. `jakc drop <name>` writes it.
;;
;; On Geyser Rock (level training) the bomb also drops by itself, on a fixed spot of a table (see "the drop spots": the bridge, and
;; the blue eco vent before the precursor door), the first time Jak walks within *gauntlet-bridge-trigger-radius* of it, and
;; again only after he has been farther than *gauntlet-bridge-rearm-range* away. Only one bomb is alive at a time.
;;
;; The mod speaks in eco: the colour of a charge says what a hazard does, red strength and blue draw. See "the eco charge"
;; below; the bomb is blue, some of the stampede's yakows are red, and babaks (babak.gc, on every level) are born red or blue.
;;
;; The same request also sends a herd of yakows charging at Jak ("7 stampede"), and in Sandover (level village1) the herd
;; charges by itself, from the Forbidden Jungle side, the first time Jak comes within *gauntlet-stampede-trigger-radius*
;; of the spot beside the farmer where the player asked for it. See "the stampede" below.
;;
;; At Sentinel Beach (level beach) Klaww, the ogre boss of Mountain Pass, falls out of the sky onto the pelican as it lands at
;; its nest with the stolen power cell, and throws boulders at Jak; the buttons around the beach throw boulders back (one hit
;; each), and the cell is his to give up when he falls. The fight survives Jak dying. "klaww" in the request file drops him anywhere. See "Klaww" below.
;;
;; On every level, each scout fly box whose eco has a source in reach wears an eco colour (a table) and opens only when Jak breaks it
;; carrying that eco; a wrong try bounces him off with a burst of the box's colour. The mod makes no eco of its own: a colour is the
;; game's own eco in the level near the box, or a carrier, a lurker near the box that glows its colour and spills it where it dies and
;; comes back after a while if the box is still closed. Green is the zoomer's eco and is on Precursor Basin only; a box with no colour it
;; can get is an ordinary scout fly box. The game asks the box through a hook in engine/common-obs/crates.gc. See "the scout fly boxes".
;;
;; The skull TNT barrels of Mountain Pass stand wherever a table of spots puts them (the first is on Sentinel Beach, between a
;; power cell and the spot below it): touch one and Jak dies, and it explodes. A barrel that is gone is stood again once Jak
;; is far from it. See "the TNT barrels" below.
;;
;; Also at Sentinel Beach, each time a lurkerworm rises out of the sand it pulls Snowy Mountain's ice cubes up out of the ground
;; around it (*gauntlet-worm-cube-count* of them), tinted sand. They are ordinary ice cubes from then on. The worm raises them
;; in levels/beach/lurkerworm.gc; ice-cube.gc is in GAME.CGO for it. The settings are only declared here.
;;
;; On every level, each enemy that runs on the nav mesh (a babak, a lurker crab, a hopper...) is born with company: itself and
;; clones born beside it by the same init, *gauntlet-lurker-multiplier* of them in all. See "the horde" below; the hook that
;; hears of each birth is in engine/entity/entity.gc.
;;
;; On Misty Island (level misty) the muse decides how the island behaves: caught, the island is calm, the lurkers it places and nothing
;; more, at their own pace and as charged as babak-charge-chance makes them; loose (not yet caught, or dropped by a hit, a bonk or a
;; death), it is mayhem: those lurkers with their company (the horde's clones) and the mayhem's extras, faster, babaks charged. A portrait of
;; her face in a corner of the hud shows which. See "the muse" and "the muse's body" below.
;;
;; The bomb is the big dark eco bomb Gol and Maia's robot drops in the final
;; boss (darkecobomb, levels/finalboss/robotboss-weapon.gc), made available
;; outside the Citadel:
;;   - its art group is in GAME.CGO (common_art_groups in the decompiler config,
;;     darkecobomb-ag.go and the tpages it needs in game.gd), and its skelgroup
;;     asks for texture level 2 so it is found there;
;;   - its blast and warning particles are copied below from robotboss-part.gc
;;     under new ids, because that file only loads with FIN.DGO. The textures
;;     are all from the common "effects" tpage;
;;   - its sounds are COMMON.SBK ones: bomb-open and robo-warning are what the
;;     finale itself plays, and the blast is "explosion", the one the misty
;;     balloon lurker's mine makes. The finale's own blast sound, explod-bomb,
;;     lives in FINALBOS.SBK and would be silent here.
;;
;; The bomb pulls Jak in, which in the eco language is blue: its body glows blue and trails Jak's blue eco aura.
;;
;; It also draws its blast on the ground, in the one language the mod has for an area that will hurt (see gauntlet-ring), whose
;; rule is: get out before the inner ring reaches you. From the moment the bomb appears, a red wall stands at the blast radius
;; around where it will land, pulsing quicker as the countdown runs down. When the countdown starts a ring grows from the middle
;; and reaches the wall as the bomb goes off, and the ground it has swept glows: that ground is already the blast's. The blast
;; radius is far wider than a boulder's, so the ground is probed once, when the bomb appears, and the circles follow it.
;;
;; The bomb is a brain (gauntlet-bomb, a bare process-drawable that falls,
;; counts down and goes off) with a manipy for a body, the game's own way to put
;; a character on screen from code (the Yellow Sage does the same in
;; levels/training/training-obs.gc). The body has no collision of its own, so
;; there is nothing to stand on, push against or get stuck in. It does two things to Jak:
;;   - while it counts down it pulls him toward it, like gravity, so that the jump he knows
;;     (off a Geyser Rock pillar, say) is dragged short and the runner has something to deal
;;     with besides the clock. The pull is the game's own way of moving Jak from outside, the
;;     sunken whirlpool's and the moving platforms': a collision-checked step each frame
;;     (fill-cache-for-shape! then integrate-and-collide!, status restored after), never a write
;;     to his velocity, which his own control recomputes every frame. Standing or running on the
;;     ground he is only nudged; in the air nothing grips him and the pull builds as fast as
;;     gravity would;
;;   - when it explodes it kills him, with his normal death, if he is within the blast
;;     (unless a recent hit still has him invulnerable).

(defconstant GAUNTLET_DROP_POLL_FRAMES 30) ;; how often the request file is looked at, about twice a second
;; The tunables (countdown, radii, the pull, the drop spots, the dummies' volleys) are globals with their defaults in
;; gauntlet-h.gc. The pull's design, for reading them against: Jak's top run speed is 10 m/s (target-speed of *walk-mods*,
;; surface-h.gc) and a running jump 10 to 16 m/s (*jump-mods*, *forward-jump-mods*), against gravity of 60 m/s^2
;; (GRAVITY_AMOUNT). A runner who starts under the bomb covers 40 m in the countdown against a 35 m blast, so the pull on
;; foot must cost him under 5 m in all.
(defconstant GAUNTLET_BOMB_FIRST_TICK 0.9) ;; the finale's warning curve: the first beep when the clock reaches this cosine
(defconstant GAUNTLET_BOMB_TICK_STEP 0.06) ;; and each beep lowers the bar by this much, so they come faster and faster
(defconstant GAUNTLET_GROUND_PROBE_UP (meters 2)) ;; the ground under Jak is searched for from this far above his feet
(defconstant GAUNTLET_GROUND_PROBE_LENGTH (meters 20)) ;; ... and this far down
(defconstant GAUNTLET_BOMB_RING_PROBE_RAISE (meters 4)) ;; the ground around where the bomb lands is searched for from this far above the ground under it, so a rise in the ground does not bury the search
(defconstant GAUNTLET_PART_GROUP_BLAST 1000) ;; ids this file adds to the particle tables, above any the game uses
(defconstant GAUNTLET_PART_GROUP_TICK 1001)

